content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-21100",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 4.2 mm/s: the applicable HF-300 limit is Figure 3, vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings, with the highest reading from both housings classified. Provided the report uses that measurement basis, 4.2 is in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), 'Long-term operation'. It is below Zone C at 4.5–7.1 ('Restricted — plan maintenance') and below Zone D starting at 7.1 ('Damage likely — stop the pump'); therefore this reading alone does not trigger the highest-zone immediate-stop and reliability-engineer notification rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 74 C: the applicable HF-300 specification is normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C and trip 90 C, with temperature measured on the housing surface. Thus 74 C is 4 C above normal, but remains 6 C below alarm and 16 C below trip. The site requirement for a priority-1 work order applies only above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so 74 C does not trigger that requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Non-drive-end bearing grinding noise: there is no numerical noise limit, but Section 5.3 explicitly requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. The bearing-replacement trigger therefore applies independently of the Zone B vibration classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal condition: the HF-300 has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and the manual says 'never run dry'. The report wording 'Seal is dry' does not establish whether there is simply no visible leakage or whether the seal has run without flush. No numerical dryness limit or dry-running duration is supplied, so seal replacement is not included in the base scope without clarification or inspection findings.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: non-drive-end bearing wear or damage. Bearing wear is a documented cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, and the reported grinding noise directly meets the manual's bearing-pair replacement criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment: documented as a possible cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature; check alignment and repeat laser alignment after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing: a documented possible cause of high bearing temperature; check grease quantity during diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Less specifically supported but to be excluded: impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation/inadequate NPSH, which are documented possible causes of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before further operation or additional testing, clarify the seal statement and confirm whether Plan 11 discharge flush is available; do not run the seal dry. Validate that the vibration value is RMS velocity, obtain readings from both bearing housings for highest-reading classification, and identify which housing reached 74 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, drain and vent, and obtain the line-break permit before internal pump or seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is removed, exploit the back pull-out design without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the site's 25 kg lifting threshold: prepare a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect and record the condition of both bearings and the impeller, check grease quantity and existing alignment, and check NPSH as part of the high-vibration diagnosis. Use these findings to distinguish bearing wear from misalignment, over-greasing, impeller damage/imbalance and cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Because the non-drive-end bearing is noisy, replace both bearings as a pair: non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3) and drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3). Do not replace only the noisy bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit new casing gasket HF3-120. If seal replacement is subsequently authorised, follow Section 5.2: remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut and impeller; withdraw the seal and sleeve; inspect the sleeve for scoring; fit new component seal HF3-450 and a new casing gasket. HF3-450, not bulletin seal HF3-450B, is the documented selection for this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, use Table 5 with lightly oiled threads, applying each value only to fasteners actually disturbed: bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm; casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; and, if this asset's component seal is replaced, seal gland nuts M10 to 25 Nm. The 30 Nm HF3-450B bulletin torque does not apply to serial HF3-21100.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the seal flush arrangement and do not run dry. Reinstate weekly vibration measurement on both bearing housings and classify the highest result using Figure 3. If a subsequent reading enters Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if housing temperature rises above 80 C, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; required as one half of the mandatory bearing-pair replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with the non-drive-end bearing even though the reported noise is non-drive-end.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; conditional on casing opening, but mandatory replacement whenever the casing is opened and also required with seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Component mechanical seal; conditional part only if clarification or inspection establishes that seal replacement is required. This is the documented seal for serial HF3-21100, rather than HF3-450B.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves; and a line-break permit, with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds the 25 kg lifting threshold. Use a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment whenever that assembly is lifted.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the line is chemically dosed, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. Chemical dosing is not stated in the fault report and must be confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The numerical readings do not currently meet the documented automatic-stop or priority-1 triggers. Nevertheless, if 'Seal is dry' means loss of flush or dry running, keep the pump out of service until that condition is corrected because the manufacturer says never to run it dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration subsequently reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D beginning at 7.1 mm/s RMS, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing temperature subsequently rises above the 80 C manufacturer alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Base scope — bearing replacement as a pair: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Base scope — laser alignment: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Base bearing-and-alignment scope totals 7.5 task-hours and 13.5 technician-hours from Table 6. This is not a complete outage-duration estimate because no standard times are supplied for diagnosis, isolation, lifting, inspection or recommissioning.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional scope only: if mechanical seal replacement is authorised, add the Table 6 allowance of 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland torque conflict: SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, requires HF3-450B and 30 Nm only for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-111 is serial HF3-21100 and is therefore outside that range. The bulletin expressly says pumps below HF3-22000 continue using HF3-450 and manual Table 5; consequently this asset uses HF3-450 and M10 gland nuts at 25 Nm with lightly oiled threads if seal work is performed, not the bulletin part or 30 Nm torque.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-sleeve decision: the bulletin instruction to replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm is contained within its instructions for pumps at HF3-22000 and above, so it is not an applicable acceptance limit for HF3-21100. The manual requires inspection of the sleeve for scoring but supplies no numerical rejection threshold for this serial; do not transfer the bulletin threshold without further engineering guidance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does 'Seal is dry' mean no external leakage, or that the seal/pump has run dry or lost Plan 11 flush? Has any dry running occurred, for how long, and is the pump currently stopped? This determines whether conditional seal work is needed and whether further operation is prohibited (C02, C09).",
    "Is the 4.2 mm/s vibration value RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what are the separate drive-end and non-drive-end readings? Figure 3 classification requires the highest reading from both housings (C06, C07).",
    "Which bearing housing reached 74 C, and was the value measured on the housing surface as specified? Were both housings at the same temperature (C01, C02)?",
    "Is the suction or discharge line chemically dosed, thereby triggering chemical goggles and nitrile gloves (C15)?",
    "The supplied excerpts do not give the detailed bearing disassembly/reassembly method, bearing installation requirements, grease type or specified grease quantity. Obtain the applicable procedure before bearing work; also confirm whether the planned bearing access will disturb the casing or seal so that conditional parts and labour can be finalised (C09, C10).",
    "If seal work is required, what is the shaft sleeve's measured condition and the applicable scoring rejection limit for serial HF3-21100? The supplied manual only says to inspect for scoring, and the 0.1 mm bulletin threshold is scoped to higher serials (C10, C13).",
    "The evidence defines the priority-1 trigger above the temperature alarm but supplies no site definitions for P2/P3 or a required completion date. P2 is therefore a planning judgement based on the noisy bearing and above-normal temperature, not a documented site priority classification (C10, C15)."
  ]
}
